BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:AVL Writers
UID:event_316829565@meetup.com
SEQUENCE:1
DTSTAMP:20261010T052959Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261010T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261010T140000
SUMMARY:October Write-A-Thon
DESCRIPTION:AVL Writers\nJoin AVL Writers for an independent writing sessi
 on. Unlike the usual events\, this will be an independently focused writin
 g session held at Odd’s Cafe. This isn’t about sharing your writing. I
 t’s about having a time and place to work on it with minimal distraction
 .\n\nSilence or headphones encouraged\, but light conversation can always 
 happen\, so be ready for it. All writers welcome regardless of experience 
 level.\n\nIntroductions will occur at the beginning of the session and you
 ’re encouraged to show up a good few minutes before. Five-minute breaks 
 will be announced and recommended at every hour interval to help everyone 
 keep pace. Don’t worry about staying all four hours. Feel free to show u
 p or leave at your leisure.\n\nIf you're having trouble finding us\, look 
 for a placard on the table with the group's name or ask the staff (they wi
 ll point us out). Please support Odd’s Cafe by purchasing one or more it
 ems as you work\, as they’ve been supportive of this group for quite a l
 ong time.\n\n**If you would like to join our group email list for updates 
 regarding contests\, events\, and to request to join the group Discord\, y
 ou can [sign up on our website](https://avlwriters.com/).**
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/avl-writers/events/316829565/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20261003T173424Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20261003T173424Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:AVL Writers
UID:event_316700500@meetup.com
SEQUENCE:1
DTSTAMP:20261010T052959Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261014T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261014T200000
SUMMARY:Weekly Critique
DESCRIPTION:AVL Writers\nThis is the standing weekly critique. Bring anyth
 ing new you're working on to share with the group. If you don't have a pro
 ject to share\, you are most welcome to attend\, discuss\, and get inspire
 d.\n\nFor our group discussion\, please bring at least 8-10 printed copies
  of your piece. That way\, we can all read through each other's work and p
 rovide feedback.\n\nSharing our creative efforts is an important part of t
 he writing process. I'm really looking forward to reading what you've been
  working on. Don't worry if it's still a rough draft.\n\nIf you're having 
 trouble finding us\, look for a placard on the table with the group's name
 .\n\nIf you would like to join our group email list for updates regarding 
 contests\, events\, and more [you can sign up on our website](https://avlw
 riters.com/).
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/avl-writers/events/316700500/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260924T222502Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260924T222502Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
